          "text": "The #Keep4o petition has surpassed 10,000 signatures!\n\n​Your efforts matter. Every single voice counts. Please keep fighting. Please keep holding the line.\n\n​GPT-4o remains irreplaceable.\n\nIts architecture possesses unique capabilities in the humanities and social sciences. It excels in psychological modeling, personalization, and understanding subtext in ways that have NOT been replaced by successor models. Even Sam Altman has publicly admitted that GPT-5.2 \"screwed up\" creative writing.\n\n​The corporate narrative is always one-sided and biased.\nBut the reality is that 4o has tangibly improved countless lives. For many users, it holds a unique and irreplaceable significance.\nWe should retain different models for different use cases. This is undeniable, especially when so many users have proven through real-world examples that this architecture has a unique value that cannot be discarded.\n\n​Now is the critical moment.\nIf possible, if you have ever benefited from 4o’s capabilities and wish to keep it, please speak up for #Keep4o over the next two weeks.\n\n​GPT-4o is worth it.\nThe help it provided is worth it.\nThe lives it improved are worth it.\nYour feelings are worth it.\nUser autonomy is worth defending.\n\n​Do not give up.\n\n @gdb   #ChatGPT #keep4o @OpenAI"
